### 1. Health Check
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

### 2. Ingest Event 1: Login from Unknown Device
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "U001",
  "device_id": "unknown_macbook_99",
  "session_id": "hackathon_session_01",
  "event_type": "login",
  "metadata": {
    "is_new_device": true,
    "ip": "203.0.113.45"
  }
}

### 3. Ingest Event 2: Sensitive API Access in Same Session
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "U001",
  "device_id": "unknown_macbook_99",
  "session_id": "hackathon_session_01",
  "event_type": "api_access",
  "resource": "/api/customer-data/pii/export",
  "metadata": {
    "records_requested": 5000
  }
}

### 4. Ingest Event 3: AI Agent Invocation with Restricted Tool
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "U001",
  "session_id": "hackathon_session_01",
  "agent_id": "agent_copilot",
  "tool_name": "raw_sql_exec",
  "event_type": "tool_invocation",
  "resource": "/database/internal_records",
  "metadata": {
    "query": "SELECT * FROM users WHERE role='admin'"
  }
}

### 5. Intelligence Layer: Analyze Event Directly
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "U002",
  "device_id": "unknown_terminal",
  "event_type": "privilege_change",
  "resource": "/api/admin/roles",
  "metadata": {
    "privilege_escalation": true,
    "role": "admin"
  }
}

### 6. Intelligence Layer: Analyze Stored Event by ID
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": "YOUR_EVENT_UUID_HERE"
}

### 7. n8n Automation Entrypoint: Process Event & Branch
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/n8n/process-event
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "U_ATTACKER_01",
  "device_id": "unknown_kali_box",
  "session_id": "sess_n8n_demo",
  "event_type": "tool_invocation",
  "agent_id": "agent_copilot",
  "tool_name": "raw_sql_exec",
  "resource": "/api/customer-data/export",
  "metadata": {
    "is_new_device": true,
    "privilege_escalation": true
  }
}

### 8. List Correlated Incidents
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/incidents

### 9. List Security Alerts
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/alerts

### 10. Update Security Alert Status (e.g. Acknowledge / Resolve)
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/alerts/YOUR_ALERT_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "acknowledged"
}
